<?php

return [
    // Overview
    'Insecure deserialization' => 'Deserialisasi tidak aman',
    "In this section, we'll cover what insecure deserialization is and describe how it can potentially expose websites to high-severity attacks. We'll highlight typical scenarios and demonstrate some widely applicable techniques using concrete examples of PHP, Ruby, and Java deserialization. We'll also look at some ways that you can avoid insecure deserialization vulnerabilities in your own websites." => 'Pada bagian ini, kami membahas apa itu deserialisasi tidak aman, risiko serangan berat yang ditimbulkannya, contoh teknik di PHP, Ruby, dan Java, serta cara pencegahannya.',
    "If you're already familiar with the basic concepts behind deserialization vulnerabilities and just want to practice exploiting them on some realistic, deliberately vulnerable targets, you can access all of the labs in this topic from the link below." => 'Jika Anda sudah memahami konsep dasar kerentanan deserialisasi dan ingin berlatih eksploitasi pada target realistis, akses semua lab topik ini lewat tautan di bawah.',
    'View all deserialization labs' => 'Lihat semua lab deserialisasi',
    'What is serialization?' => 'Apa itu serialisasi?',
    '<strong>Serialization</strong> is the process of converting complex data structures, such as objects and their fields, into a "flatter" format that can be sent and received as a sequential stream of bytes. Serializing data makes it much simpler to:' => '<strong>Serialisasi</strong> adalah proses mengubah struktur data kompleks seperti objek beserta atributnya menjadi format datar berupa aliran byte berurutan agar mudah untuk:',
    'Write complex data to inter-process memory, a file, or a database' => 'Menyimpan objek kompleks ke memori antarproses, berkas, atau basis data',
    'Send complex data, for example, over a network, between different components of an application, or in an API call' => 'Mengirim data objek melalui jaringan, antar-komponen aplikasi, atau panggilan API',
    "Crucially, when serializing an object, its state is also persisted. In other words, the object's attributes are preserved, along with their assigned values." => 'Seluruh kondisi (state) atribut objek dan nilainya ikut disimpan dalam hasil serialisasi.',
    'Serialization vs deserialization' => 'Serialisasi vs deserialisasi',
    "<strong>Deserialization</strong> is the process of restoring this byte stream to a fully functional replica of the original object, in the exact state as when it was serialized. The website's logic can then interact with this deserialized object, just like it would with any other object." => '<strong>Deserialisasi</strong> memulihkan aliran byte tersebut kembali menjadi objek utuh di memori dengan state persis seperti saat diserialisasi.',
    'Many programming languages offer native support for serialization. Exactly how objects are serialized depends on the language. Some languages serialize objects into binary formats, whereas others use different string formats, with varying degrees of human readability. Note that all of the original object\'s attributes are stored in the serialized data stream, including any private fields. To prevent a field from being serialized, it must be explicitly marked as "transient" in the class declaration.' => 'Format serialisasi bergantung bahasanya (biner atau string), dan seluruh atribut termasuk field privat ikut tersimpan kecuali ditandai transient.',
    'Be aware that when working with different programming languages, serialization may be referred to as marshalling (Ruby) or pickling (Python). These terms are synonymous with "serialization" in this context.' => 'Pada bahasa lain proses ini kadang disebut marshalling (Ruby) atau pickling (Python).',
    'What is insecure deserialization?' => 'Apa itu deserialisasi tidak aman?',
    'Insecure deserialization is when user-controllable data is deserialized by a website. This potentially enables an attacker to manipulate serialized objects in order to pass harmful data into the application code.' => 'Deserialisasi tidak aman terjadi saat aplikasi mendeserialisasi data yang bisa dikendalikan pengguna sehingga penyerang dapat menyuntikkan objek termanipulasi ke aplikasi.',
    'It is even possible to replace a serialized object with an object of an entirely different class. Alarmingly, objects of any class that is available to the website will be deserialized and instantiated, regardless of which class was expected. For this reason, insecure deserialization is sometimes known as an "object injection" vulnerability.' => 'Penyerang bahkan bisa mengganti tipe kelasnya dengan kelas lain mana saja yang tersedia di aplikasi (dikenal juga sebagai object injection).',
    "An object of an unexpected class might cause an exception. By this time, however, the damage may already be done. Many deserialization-based attacks are completed <strong>before</strong> deserialization is finished. This means that the deserialization process itself can initiate an attack, even if the website's own functionality does not directly interact with the malicious object. For this reason, websites whose logic is based on strongly typed languages can also be vulnerable to these techniques." => 'Meskipun tipe yang salah akhirnya memicu exception, efek serangan sering sudah tereksekusi <strong>saat</strong> proses deserialisasi berlangsung lewat magic method.',
    'How do insecure deserialization vulnerabilities arise?' => 'Bagaimana celah deserialisasi tidak aman muncul?',
    'Insecure deserialization typically arises because there is a general lack of understanding of how dangerous deserializing user-controllable data can be. Ideally, user input should never be deserialized at all.' => 'Idealnya data dari pengguna tidak pernah dideserialisasi menggunakan format serialisasi objek.',
    'However, sometimes website owners think they are safe because they implement some form of additional check on the deserialized data. This approach is often ineffective because it is virtually impossible to implement validation or sanitization to account for every eventuality. These checks are also fundamentally flawed as they rely on checking the data after it has been deserialized, which in many cases will be too late to prevent the attack.' => 'Memeriksa tipe objek setelah deserialisasi selesai sudah terlambat karena kode di magic method berjalan lebih awal.',
    'Vulnerabilities may also arise because deserialized objects are often assumed to be trustworthy. Especially when using languages with a binary serialization format, developers might think that users cannot read or manipulate the data effectively. However, while it may require more effort, it is just as possible for an attacker to exploit binary serialized objects as it is to exploit string-based formats.' => 'Format biner juga tidak memberikan perlindungan apa pun karena tetap bisa dibaca, dibuat ulang, dan dimodifikasi oleh penyerang.',
    'Deserialization-based attacks are also made possible due to the number of dependencies that exist in modern websites. A typical site might implement many different libraries, which each have their own dependencies as well. This creates a massive pool of classes and methods that is difficult to manage securely. As an attacker can create instances of any of these classes, it is hard to predict which methods can be invoked on the malicious data. This is especially true if an attacker is able to chain together a long series of unexpected method invocations, passing data into a sink that is completely unrelated to the initial source. It is, therefore, almost impossible to anticipate the flow of malicious data and plug every potential hole.' => 'Ratusan kelas dari dependensi pustaka pihak ketiga membentuk koleksi luas kelas yang dapat dirangkai menjadi rantai gadget berbahaya.',
    'In short, it can be argued that it is not possible to securely deserialize untrusted input.' => 'Singkatnya, mendeserialisasi input tak tepercaya secara langsung nyaris mustahil dibuat aman sepenuhnya.',
    'What is the impact of insecure deserialization?' => 'Apa dampak deserialisasi tidak aman?',
    'The impact of insecure deserialization can be very severe because it provides an entry point to a massively increased attack surface. It allows an attacker to reuse existing application code in harmful ways, resulting in numerous other vulnerabilities, often remote code execution.' => 'Dampaknya kerap sangat fatal, sering berujung pada remote code execution lewat pemakaian ulang kelas kode yang sudah ada.',
    'Even in cases where remote code execution is not possible, insecure deserialization can lead to privilege escalation, arbitrary file access, and denial-of-service attacks.' => 'Bila RCE tak tercapai sekalipun, celah ini tetap dapat menghasilkan eskalasi hak istimewa, penghapusan/pembacaan file sembarang, dan denial of service.',
    'How to exploit insecure deserialization vulnerabilities' => 'Cara mengeksploitasi deserialisasi tidak aman',
    "Now that you're familiar with the basics of serialization and deserialization, we can look at how you can exploit insecure deserialization vulnerabilities." => 'Pelajari teknik eksploitasi dari manipulasi atribut sederhana hingga rantai gadget lengkap di panduan berikut.',
    'Exploiting insecure deserialization vulnerabilities' => 'Mengeksploitasi kerentanan deserialisasi tidak aman',
    'How to prevent insecure deserialization vulnerabilities' => 'Cara mencegah kerentanan deserialisasi tidak aman',
    'Generally speaking, deserialization of user input should be avoided unless absolutely necessary. The high severity of exploits that it potentially enables, and the difficulty in protecting against them, outweigh the benefits in many cases.' => 'Hindari deserialisasi input pengguna dan pilih format pertukaran data sederhana seperti JSON.',
    'If you do need to deserialize data from untrusted sources, incorporate robust measures to make sure that the data has not been tampered with. For example, you could implement a digital signature to check the integrity of the data. However, remember that any checks must take place <strong>before</strong> beginning the deserialization process. Otherwise, they are of little use.' => 'Jika benar-benar terpaksa, verifikasi tanda tangan kriptografis HMAC/digital <strong>sebelum</strong> menjalankan fungsi deserialisasi.',
    'If possible, you should avoid using generic deserialization features altogether. Serialized data from these methods contains all attributes of the original object, including private fields that potentially contain sensitive information. Instead, you could create your own class-specific serialization methods so that you can at least control which fields are exposed.' => 'Batasi kelas yang boleh diinstansiasi secara ketat lewat allowlist dan buat serialisasi khusus untuk tiap kelas bila perlu.',
    "Finally, remember that the vulnerability is the deserialization of user input, not the presence of gadget chains that subsequently handle the data. Don't rely on trying to eliminate gadget chains that you identify during testing. It is impractical to try and plug them all due to the web of cross-library dependencies that almost certainly exist on your website. At any given time, publicly documented memory corruption exploits are also a factor, meaning that your application may be vulnerable regardless." => 'Akar masalahnya ada pada proses mendeserialisasi data tak tepercaya, bukan semata keberadaan gadget chain di pustaka.',

    // exploiting
    "In this section, we'll teach you how to exploit some common scenarios using examples from PHP, Ruby, and Java deserialization. We hope to demonstrate how exploiting insecure deserialization is actually much easier than many people believe. This is even the case during blackbox testing if you are able to use pre-built gadget chains." => 'Pada bagian ini, Anda belajar mengeksploitasi deserialisasi tidak aman pada PHP, Ruby, dan Java, baik secara blackbox dengan rantai gadget siap pakai maupun penyusunan kustom.',
    "We'll also guide you through the process of creating your own high-severity deserialization-based attacks. Although these usually require source-code access, they can also be easier to learn than you might think once you understand the basic concepts. In particular, we'll cover the following topics:" => 'Topik yang dibahas meliputi:',
    '[[A0]]How to identify insecure deserialization[[/A0]] [[S0]]LABS[[/S0]]' => '[[A0]]Cara mengidentifikasi deserialisasi tidak aman[[/A0]] [[S0]]LAB PRAKTIK[[/S0]]',
    '[[A0]]Modifying serialized objects that are expected by the website[[/A0]] [[S0]]LABS[[/S0]]' => '[[A0]]Memodifikasi objek ter-serialisasi yang diharapkan situs[[/A0]] [[S0]]LAB PRAKTIK[[/S0]]',
    '[[A0]]Passing malicious data into dangerous website functionality[[/A0]] [[S0]]LABS[[/S0]]' => '[[A0]]Memanfaatkan fungsionalitas berbahaya di aplikasi[[/A0]] [[S0]]LAB PRAKTIK[[/S0]]',
    '[[A0]]Injecting arbitrary object types[[/A0]] [[S0]]LABS[[/S0]]' => '[[A0]]Menyuntikkan tipe objek sembarang[[/A0]] [[S0]]LAB PRAKTIK[[/S0]]',
    '[[A0]]Chaining method invocations to control the flow of data into dangerous sink gadgets[[/A0]] [[S0]]LABS[[/S0]]' => '[[A0]]Merangkai gadget chain menuju sink berbahaya[[/A0]] [[S0]]LAB PRAKTIK[[/S0]]',
    '[[A0]]Manually creating your own advanced exploits[[/A0]] [[S0]]LABS[[/S0]]' => '[[A0]]Menyusun eksploitasi lanjutan secara manual[[/A0]] [[S0]]LAB PRAKTIK[[/S0]]',
    '[[A0]]PHAR deserialization[[/A0]] [[S0]]LABS[[/S0]]' => '[[A0]]Deserialisasi PHAR[[/A0]] [[S0]]LAB PRAKTIK[[/S0]]',
    'Although many of the labs and examples are based on PHP, most of the exploitation techniques are equally valid for other languages as well.' => 'Meskipun banyak contoh memakai PHP, prinsip eksploitasinya berlaku luas untuk Java, Ruby, .NET, dan Python.',
    'How to identify insecure deserialization' => 'Cara mengidentifikasi deserialisasi tidak aman',
    'Identifying insecure deserialization is relatively simple regardless of whether you are whitebox or blackbox testing.' => 'Mengenali data ter-serialisasi pada trafik HTTP relatif mudah di pengujian whitebox maupun blackbox.',
    'During auditing, you should look at all data being passed into the website and try to identify anything that looks like serialized data. Serialized data can be identified relatively easily if you know the format that different languages use. In this section, we\'ll show examples from both PHP and Java serialization. Once you identify serialized data, you can test whether you are able to control it.' => 'Periksa cookie, hidden field, dan parameter token terhadap ciri khas format serialisasi bahasa target.',
    'For users of Burp Suite Professional, Burp Scanner will automatically flag any HTTP messages that appear to contain serialized objects.' => 'Pemindai otomatis biasanya menandai cookie atau parameter yang terdeteksi berformat objek ter-serialisasi.',
    'PHP serialization format' => 'Format serialisasi PHP',
    'PHP uses a mostly human-readable string format, with letters representing the data type and numbers representing the length of each entry. For example, consider a [[C0]] object with the attributes:' => 'PHP memakai format string terbaca manusia. Misalnya objek [[C0]] berikut:',
    'When serialized, this object may look something like this:' => 'Hasil serialisasinya berbentuk seperti ini:',
    'This can be interpreted as follows:' => 'Artinya:',
    '[[C0]] - An object with the 4-character class name [[C1]]' => '[[C0]]: objek dengan nama kelas 4 karakter [[C1]]',
    '[[C0]] - the object has 2 attributes' => '[[C0]]: jumlah atribut ada 2',
    '[[C0]] - The key of the first attribute is the 4-character string [[C1]]' => '[[C0]]: nama atribut pertama string 4 karakter [[C1]]',
    '[[C0]] - The value of the first attribute is the 6-character string [[C1]]' => '[[C0]]: nilai atribut pertama string 6 karakter [[C1]]',
    '[[C0]] - The key of the second attribute is the 10-character string [[C1]]' => '[[C0]]: nama atribut kedua string 10 karakter [[C1]]',
    '[[C0]] - The value of the second attribute is the boolean value [[C1]]' => '[[C0]]: nilai atribut kedua bertipe boolean [[C1]]',
    'The native methods for PHP serialization are [[C0]] and [[C1]]. If you have source code access, you should start by looking for [[C2]] anywhere in the code and investigating further.' => 'Fungsi bawaannya adalah [[C0]] dan [[C1]]. Saat meninjau kode sumber, cari seluruh pemanggilan [[C2]].',
    'Java serialization format' => 'Format serialisasi Java',
    'Some languages, such as Java, use binary serialization formats. This is more difficult to read, but you can still identify serialized data if you know how to recognize a few tell-tale signs. For example, serialized Java objects always begin with the same bytes, which are encoded as [[C0]]in hexadecimal and [[C1]] in Base64.' => 'Java memakai format biner yang selalu diawali byte ciri khas [[C0]] (hex) atau awalan [[C1]] jika di-encode Base64.',
    'Any class that implements the interface [[C0]] can be serialized and deserialized. If you have source code access, take note of any code that uses the [[C1]] method, which is used to read and deserialize data from an [[C2]].' => 'Semua kelas pengimplementasi [[C0]] dapat diserialisasi; cari penggunaan [[C1]] atas [[C2]] pada audit kode.',
    'Manipulating serialized objects' => 'Memanipulasi objek ter-serialisasi',
    'Exploiting some deserialization vulnerabilities can be as easy as changing an attribute in a serialized object. As the object state is persisted, you can study the serialized data to identify and edit interesting attribute values. You can then pass the malicious object into the website via its deserialization process. This is the initial step for a basic deserialization exploit.' => 'Bentuk eksploitasi paling sederhana cukup mengubah nilai atribut objek ter-serialisasi.',
    'Broadly speaking, there are two approaches you can take when manipulating serialized objects. You can either edit the object directly in its byte stream form, or you can write a short script in the corresponding language to create and serialize the new object yourself. The latter approach is often easier when working with binary serialization formats.' => 'Anda dapat menyunting string ter-serialisasi langsung atau memakai skrip bahasa terkait untuk membangun objek biner baru.',
    'Modifying object attributes' => 'Mengubah atribut objek',
    'When tampering with the data, as long as the attacker preserves a valid serialized object, the deserialization process will create a server-side object with the modified attribute values.' => 'Selama struktur panjang byte valid, server membuat instansi objek dengan nilai modifikasi.',
    "As a simple example, consider a website that uses a serialized [[C0]] object to store data about a user's session in a cookie. If an attacker spotted this serialized object in an HTTP request, they might decode it to find the following byte stream:" => 'Misalnya cookie menyimpan objek [[C0]] ter-serialisasi seperti ini:',
    'The [[C0]] attribute is an obvious point of interest. An attacker could simply change the boolean value of the attribute to [[C1]] (true), re-encode the object, and overwrite their current cookie with this modified value. In isolation, this has no effect. However, let\'s say the website uses this cookie to check whether the current user has access to certain administrative functionality:' => 'Cukup ganti [[C0]] menjadi [[C1]] (true) dan encode ulang bila aplikasi mengandalkan objek cookie ini untuk memeriksa hak admin:',
    'This vulnerable code would instantiate a [[C0]] object based on the data from the cookie, including the attacker-modified [[C1]] attribute. At no point is the authenticity of the serialized object checked. This data is then passed into the conditional statement and, in this case, would allow for an easy privilege escalation.' => 'Karena tak ada validasi tanda tangan cookie, objek [[C0]] dengan atribut [[C1]] palsu langsung diterima untuk eskalasi hak.',
    'This simple scenario is not common in the wild. However, editing an attribute value in this way demonstrates the first step towards accessing the massive amount of attack-surface exposed by insecure deserialization.' => 'Meski skenario sederhana jarang dijumpai apa adanya, teknik ini menjadi pijakan awal memahami manipulasi objek.',
    'Modifying data types' => 'Mengubah tipe data',
    'We\'ve seen how you can modify attribute values in serialized objects, but it\'s also possible to supply unexpected data types.' => 'Anda juga bisa mengubah tipe data properti objek (misalnya string menjadi integer).',
    'PHP-based logic is particularly vulnerable to this kind of manipulation due to the behavior of its loose comparison operator ([[C0]]) when comparing different data types. For example, if you perform a loose comparison between an integer and a string, PHP will attempt to convert the string to an integer, meaning that [[C1]] evaluates to [[C2]].' => 'Operator perbandingan longgar PHP ([[C0]]) memicu konversi tipe otomatis sehingga [[C1]] bernilai [[C2]].',
    'Unusually, this also works for any alphanumeric string that starts with a number. In this case, PHP will effectively convert the entire string to an integer value based on the initial number. The rest of the string is ignored completely. Therefore, [[C0]]is in practice treated as [[C1]].' => 'String yang diawali angka ikut dikonversi, sehingga [[C0]] dievaluasi setara [[C1]].',
    'Likewise, on PHP 7.x and earlier the comparison [[C0]] evaluates to [[C1]], because PHP treats the entire string as the integer [[C2]].' => 'Di PHP 7.x ke bawah, [[C0]] juga bernilai [[C1]] karena string non-numerik dianggap bernilai [[C2]].',
    'Consider a case where this loose comparison operator is used in conjunction with user-controllable data from a deserialized object. This could potentially result in dangerous logic flaws.' => 'Perhatikan contoh logika rentan berbasis perbandingan longgar berikut:',
    'Let\'s say an attacker modified the password attribute so that it contained the integer [[C0]] instead of the expected string. As long as the stored password does not start with a number, the condition would always return [[C1]], enabling an authentication bypass. Note that this is only possible because deserialization preserves the data type. If the code fetched the password from the request directly, the [[C2]] would be converted to a string and the condition would evaluate to [[C3]].' => 'Mengubah tipe atribut token atau sandi menjadi integer [[C0]] membuat kondisi selalu [[C1]] dibanding [[C2]]/[[C3]] pada input form HTTP biasa karena deserialisasi menjaga tipe data asli.',
    'In PHP 8 and later, the [[C0]] comparison evaluates to [[C1]] because strings are no longer implicitly converted to [[C2]] during comparisons. As a result, this exploit is not possible on these versions of PHP.' => 'Mulai PHP 8, perbandingan [[C0]] mengembalikan [[C1]] dan tidak lagi otomatis dianggap [[C2]].',
    'The behavior when comparing an alphanumeric string that starts with a number remains the same in PHP 8. As such, [[C0]] is still treated as [[C1]].' => 'Namun perbandingan string yang diawali angka seperti [[C0]] tetap diperlakukan sebagai [[C1]].',
    'Be aware that when modifying data types in any serialized object format, it is important to remember to update any type labels and length indicators in the serialized data too. Otherwise, the serialized object will be corrupted and will not be deserialized.' => 'Pastikan penanda tipe dan panjang karakter ikut diperbarui agar struktur objek tidak rusak.',
    'When working directly with binary formats, we recommend using the Hackvertor extension, available from the BApp store. With Hackvertor, you can modify the serialized data as a string, and it will automatically update the binary data, adjusting the offsets accordingly. This can save you a lot of manual effort.' => 'Untuk format biner, alat bantu pengubah tipe otomatis dapat menyesuaikan offset byte tanpa merusak struktur.',
    'Using application functionality' => 'Memanfaatkan fungsionalitas aplikasi',
    "As well as simply checking attribute values, a website's functionality might also perform dangerous operations on data from a deserialized object. In this case, you can use insecure deserialization to pass in unexpected data and leverage the related functionality to do damage." => 'Aplikasi kerap mengumpankan atribut dari objek hasil deserialisasi langsung ke fungsi sistem berkas atau kueri.',
    'For example, as part of a website\'s "Delete user" functionality, the user\'s profile picture is deleted by accessing the file path in the [[C0]] attribute. If this [[C1]] was created from a serialized object, an attacker could exploit this by passing in a modified object with the [[C2]] set to an arbitrary file path. Deleting their own user account would then delete this arbitrary file as well.' => 'Jika fitur hapus akun membaca [[C0]] pada objek [[C1]], mengubah [[C2]] menjadi path berkas sistem bisa menghapus file target saat akun sendiri dihapus.',
    'This example relies on the attacker manually invoking the dangerous method via user-accessible functionality. However, insecure deserialization becomes much more interesting when you create exploits that pass data into dangerous methods automatically. This is enabled by the use of "magic methods".' => 'Efek jauh lebih besar muncul ketika metode dipanggil otomatis oleh "magic method" saat deserialisasi.',
    'Magic methods' => 'Magic method',
    'Magic methods are a special subset of methods that you do not have to explicitly invoke. Instead, they are invoked automatically whenever a particular event or scenario occurs. Magic methods are a common feature of object-oriented programming in various languages. They are sometimes indicated by prefixing or surrounding the method name with double-underscores.' => 'Magic method adalah metode khusus (seperti metode berawalan __ di PHP) yang dipanggil otomatis oleh runtime pada momen tertentu tanpa dipanggil eksplisit.',
    'Developers can add magic methods to a class in order to predetermine what code should be executed when the corresponding event or scenario occurs. Exactly when and why a magic method is invoked differs from method to method. One of the most common examples in PHP is [[C0]], which is invoked whenever an object of the class is instantiated, similar to Python\'s [[C1]]. Typically, constructor magic methods like this contain code to initialize the attributes of the instance. However, magic methods can be customized by developers to execute any code they want.' => 'Misalnya [[C0]] di PHP atau [[C1]] di Python yang berjalan otomatis saat instansiasi.',
    'Magic methods are widely used and do not represent a vulnerability on their own. But they can become dangerous when the code that they execute handles attacker-controllable data, for example, from a deserialized object. This can be exploited by an attacker to automatically invoke methods on the deserialized data when the corresponding conditions are met.' => 'Magic method menjadi berbahaya saat memproses properti objek yang dapat diisi penyerang sebelum atau sesudah deserialisasi.',
    'Most importantly in this context, some languages have magic methods that are invoked automatically <strong>during</strong> the deserialization process. For example, PHP\'s [[C0]] method looks for and invokes an object\'s [[C1]] magic method.' => 'Di PHP, fungsi [[C0]] memicu [[C1]] secara otomatis <strong>selama</strong> deserialisasi.',
    'In Java deserialization, the same applies to the [[C0]] method, which is used to read data from the initial byte stream and essentially acts like a constructor for "re-initializing" a serialized object. However, [[C1]] classes can also declare their own [[C2]] method as follows:' => 'Pada Java, selain [[C0]], kelas [[C1]] boleh menuliskan [[C2]] kustom yang berjalan saat dibaca:',
    'A [[C0]] method declared in exactly this way acts as a magic method that is invoked during deserialization. This allows the class to control the deserialization of its own fields more closely.' => 'Metode [[C0]] berpola tepat seperti itu berjalan otomatis saat deserialisasi berlangsung.',
    "You should pay close attention to any classes that contain these types of magic methods. They allow you to pass data from a serialized object into the website's code before the object is fully deserialized. This is the starting point for creating more advanced exploits." => 'Kelas dengan magic method seperti inilah pintu awal dari hampir seluruh gadget chain.',
    'Injecting arbitrary objects' => 'Menyuntikkan tipe objek sembarang',
    "As we've seen, it is occasionally possible to exploit insecure deserialization by simply editing the object supplied by the website. However, injecting arbitrary object types can open up many more possibilities." => 'Dengan mengganti nama kelas di data ter-serialisasi, Anda dapat memanfaatkan kode kelas mana saja yang tersedia di server.',
    'In object-oriented programming, the methods available to an object are determined by its class. Therefore, if an attacker can manipulate which class of object is being passed in as serialized data, they can influence what code is executed after, and even during, deserialization.' => 'Pemilihan kelas menentukan magic method dan fungsi lanjutan apa yang langsung dieksekusi.',
    'Deserialization methods do not typically check what they are deserializing. This means that you can pass in objects of any serializable class that is available to the website, and the object will be deserialized. This effectively allows an attacker to create instances of arbitrary classes. The fact that this object is not of the expected class does not matter. The unexpected object type might cause an exception in the application logic, but the malicious object will already be instantiated by then.' => 'Deserialisasi umum langsung menginstansiasi kelas apa pun terlebih dahulu sebelum aplikasi sempat menolak tipenya.',
    'If an attacker has access to the source code, they can study all of the available classes in detail. To construct a simple exploit, they would look for classes containing deserialization magic methods, then check whether any of them perform dangerous operations on controllable data. The attacker can then pass in a serialized object of this class to use its magic method for an exploit.' => 'Dalam audit sumber kode, cari kelas yang memiliki magic method destruksi/deserialisasi lalu lacak apakah memanggil fungsi sensitif.',
    'Classes containing these deserialization magic methods can also be used to initiate more complex attacks involving a long series of method invocations, known as a "gadget chain".' => 'Magic method juga dapat menjadi pemantik bagi rangkaian panjang pemanggilan metode bernama "gadget chain".',
    'Gadget chains' => 'Gadget chain',
    'A "gadget" is a snippet of code that exists in the application that can help an attacker to achieve a particular goal. An individual gadget may not directly do anything harmful with user input. However, the attacker\'s goal might simply be to invoke a method that will pass their input into another gadget. By chaining multiple gadgets together in this way, an attacker can potentially pass their input into a dangerous "sink gadget", where it can cause maximum damage.' => 'Gadget adalah potongan metode yang sudah ada di aplikasi atau pustaka. Merangkai beberapa gadget memungkinkan aliran data berakhir di sink gadget berbahaya seperti eksekusi perintah.',
    "It is important to understand that, unlike some other types of exploit, a gadget chain is not a payload of chained methods constructed by the attacker. All of the code already exists on the website. The only thing the attacker controls is the data that is passed into the gadget chain. This is typically done using a magic method that is invoked during deserialization, sometimes known as a \"kick-off gadget\"." => 'Penyerang tidak menyuntikkan kode baru; seluruh metode sudah tersedia di server dan dipicu oleh "kick-off gadget" menggunakan properti objek terkendali.',
    'In the wild, many insecure deserialization vulnerabilities will only be exploitable through the use of gadget chains. This can sometimes be a simple one or two-step chain, but constructing high-severity attacks will likely require a more elaborate sequence of object instantiations and method invocations. Therefore, being able to construct gadget chains is one of the key aspects of successfully exploiting insecure deserialization.' => 'Menguasai penyusunan gadget chain merupakan kunci eksploitasi deserialisasi tingkat lanjut.',
    'Working with pre-built gadget chains' => 'Memanfaatkan gadget chain siap pakai',
    'Manually identifying gadget chains can be a fairly arduous process, and is almost impossible without source code access. Fortunately, there are a few options for working with pre-built gadget chains that you can try first.' => 'Untuk pustaka umum, sering tersedia alat pembentuk payload gadget chain yang siap pakai.',
    'There are several tools available that provide a range of pre-discovered chains that have been successfully exploited on other websites. Even if you don\'t have access to the source code, you can use these tools to both identify and exploit insecure deserialization vulnerabilities with relatively little effort. This approach is made possible due to the widespread use of libraries that contain exploitable gadget chains. For example, if a gadget chain in Java\'s Apache Commons Collections library can be exploited on one website, any other website that implements this library may also be exploitable using the same chain.' => 'Alat ini memanfaatkan ketergantungan populer seperti Apache Commons atau komponen framework PHP.',
    'ysoserial' => 'ysoserial',
    'One such tool for Java deserialization is "ysoserial". This lets you choose one of the provided gadget chains for a library that you think the target application is using, then pass in a command that you want to execute. It then creates an appropriate serialized object based on the selected chain. This still involves a certain amount of trial and error, but it is considerably less labor-intensive than constructing your own gadget chains manually.' => 'Alat "ysoserial" memudahkan pembuatan payload biner Java dari daftar gadget chain pustaka populer.',
    'In Java versions 16 and above, you need to set a series of command-line arguments for Java to run ysoserial. For example:' => 'Pada Java 16 ke atas, sertakan flag --add-opens saat menjalankan ysoserial:',
    'Not all of the gadget chains in ysoserial enable you to run arbitrary code. Instead, they may be useful for other purposes. For example, you can use the following ones to help you quickly detect insecure deserialization on virtually any server:' => 'Selain RCE, tersedia gadget khusus untuk deteksi awal deserialisasi Java:',
    'The [[C0]] chain triggers a DNS lookup for a supplied URL. Most importantly, it does not rely on the target application using a specific vulnerable library and works in any known Java version. This makes it the most universal gadget chain for detection purposes. If you spot a serialized object in the traffic, you can try using this gadget chain to generate an object that triggers a DNS interaction with the Burp Collaborator server. If it does, you can be sure that deserialization occurred on your target.' => 'Rantai [[C0]] memicu DNS lookup ke domain OAST pada hampir semua versi Java tanpa butuh pustaka pihak ketiga.',
    '[[C0]] is another universal chain that you can use for initial detection. It causes the server to try establishing a TCP connection to the supplied IP address. Note that you need to provide a raw IP address rather than a hostname. This chain may be useful in environments where all outbound traffic is firewalled, including DNS lookups. You can try generating payloads with two different IP addresses: a local one and a firewalled, external one. If the application responds immediately for a payload with a local address, but hangs for a payload with an external address, causing a delay in the response, this indicates that the gadget chain worked because the server tried to connect to the firewalled address. In this case, the subtle time difference in responses can help you to detect whether deserialization occurs on the server, even in blind cases.' => '[[C0]] memicu koneksi TCP ke alamat IP langsung sehingga efektif mendeteksi lewat perbedaan jeda respons meski DNS diblokir.',
    'PHP Generic Gadget Chains' => 'PHP Generic Gadget Chains (PHPGGC)',
    'Most languages that frequently suffer from insecure deserialization vulnerabilities have equivalent proof-of-concept tools. For example, for PHP-based sites you can use "PHP Generic Gadget Chains" (PHPGGC).' => 'Untuk aplikasi PHP berbasis framework populer, alat setaranya adalah PHPGGC.',
    'It is important to note that the vulnerability is the deserialization of user-controllable data, not the mere presence of a gadget chain in the website\'s code or any of its libraries. The gadget chain is just a means of manipulating the flow of the harmful data once it has been injected. This also applies to various memory corruption vulnerabilities that rely on deserialization of untrusted data. In other words, a website may still be vulnerable even if it did somehow manage to plug every possible gadget chain.' => 'Sekali lagi, akar kerentanannya adalah menerima objek ter-serialisasi dari sumber tidak tepercaya, bukan sekadar adanya gadget chain.',
    'Working with documented gadget chains' => 'Mengadaptasi gadget chain terdokumentasi',
    'There may not always be a dedicated tool available for exploiting known gadget chains in the framework used by the target application. In this case, it\'s always worth looking online to see if there are any documented exploits that you can adapt manually. Tweaking the code may require some basic understanding of the language and framework, and you might sometimes need to serialize the object yourself, but this approach is still considerably less effort than building an exploit from scratch.' => 'Jika alat otomatis tak mendukung framework target, cari publikasi gadget chain terdokumentasi lalu sesuaikan payload-nya secara manual.',
    'Even if you can\'t find a gadget chain that\'s ready to use, you may still gain valuable knowledge that helps you create your own custom exploit.' => 'Riset terdokumentasi juga memberi petunjuk titik masuk saat merancang rantai sendiri.',
    'Creating your own exploit' => 'Menyusun eksploitasi sendiri',
    'When off-the-shelf gadget chains and documented exploits are unsuccessful, you will need to create your own exploit.' => 'Bila payload siap pakai gagal, rancang gadget chain sendiri dari kode sumber aplikasi.',
    'To successfully build your own gadget chain, you will almost certainly need source code access. The first step is to study this source code to identify a class that contains a magic method that is invoked during deserialization. Assess the code that this magic method executes to see if it directly does anything dangerous with user-controllable attributes. This is always worth checking just in case.' => 'Mulailah menelusuri setiap magic method deserialisasi (__wakeup, __destruct, readObject) di kode sumber.',
    'If the magic method is not exploitable on its own, it can serve as your "kick-off gadget" for a gadget chain. Study any methods that the kick-off gadget invokes. Do any of these do something dangerous with data that you control? If not, take a closer look at each of the methods that they subsequently invoke, and so on.' => 'Jika tidak langsung berbahaya, lacak pemanggilan metode selanjutnya yang memakai properti objek bersarang.',
    'Repeat this process, keeping track of which values you have access to, until you either reach a dead end or identify a dangerous sink gadget into which your controllable data is passed.' => 'Terus lacak aliran data antar-objek hingga mencapai sink gadget yang bisa membaca file atau mengeksekusi perintah.',
    "Once you've worked out how to successfully construct a gadget chain within the application code, the next step is to create a serialized object containing your payload. This is simply a case of studying the class declaration in the source code and creating a valid serialized object with the appropriate values required for your exploit. As we have seen in previous labs, this is relatively simple when working with string-based serialization formats." => 'Setelah jalurnya ditemukan, buat objek bersarang tersebut sesuai deklarasi kelasnya lalu serialisasi.',
    "Working with binary formats, such as when constructing a Java deserialization exploit, can be particularly cumbersome. When making minor changes to an existing object, you might be comfortable working directly with the bytes. However, when making more significant changes, such as passing in a completely new object, this quickly becomes impractical. It is often much simpler to write your own code in the target language in order to generate and serialize the data yourself." => 'Untuk format biner seperti Java, jauh lebih mudah menulis program kecil dalam bahasa tersebut guna menghasilkan aliran byte ter-serialisasi.',
    'When creating your own gadget chain, look out for opportunities to use this extra attack surface to trigger secondary vulnerabilities.' => 'Manfaatkan juga celah sekunder seperti SQL injection atau file write dari dalam properti objek.',
    "By carefully studying the source code, you can discover longer gadget chains that potentially allow you to construct high-severity attacks, often including remote code execution." => 'Analisis kode sumber secara teliti membuka jalur rantai panjang menuju eksekusi perintah jarak jauh.',
    'PHAR deserialization' => 'Deserialisasi PHAR',
    'So far, we\'ve looked primarily at exploiting deserialization vulnerabilities where the website explicitly deserializes user input. However, in PHP it is sometimes possible to exploit deserialization even if there is no obvious use of the [[C0]] method.' => 'Di PHP, deserialisasi bisa terpicu secara implisit tanpa pernah memanggil [[C0]] secara langsung.',
    'PHP provides several URL-style wrappers that you can use for handling different protocols when accessing file paths. One of these is the [[C0]] wrapper, which provides a stream interface for accessing PHP Archive ([[C1]]) files.' => 'Wrapper stream [[C0]] di PHP dipakai mengakses arsip [[C1]] (PHP Archive).',
    'The PHP documentation reveals that [[C0]] manifest files contain serialized metadata. Crucially, if you perform any filesystem operations on a [[C1]] stream, this metadata is implicitly deserialized. This means that a [[C2]] stream can potentially be a vector for exploiting insecure deserialization, provided that you can pass this stream into a filesystem method.' => 'Operasi berkas apa pun pada stream [[C1]] / [[C2]] otomatis mendeserialisasi metadata manifest [[C0]] secara tersembunyi.',
    'In the case of obviously dangerous filesystem methods, such as [[C0]] or [[C1]], websites are likely to have implemented counter-measures to reduce the potential for them to be used maliciously. However, methods such as [[C2]], which are not so overtly dangerous, may not be as well protected.' => 'Meskipun fungsi berisiko seperti [[C0]] dan [[C1]] sering dibatasi, fungsi biasa seperti [[C2]] tetap memicu deserialisasi manifest PHAR.',
    "This technique also requires you to upload the [[C0]] to the server somehow. One approach is to use an image upload functionality, for example. If you are able to create a polyglot file, with a [[C1]] masquerading as a simple [[C2]], you can sometimes bypass the website's validation checks. If you can then force the website to load this polyglot \"[[C3]]\" from a [[C4]] stream, any harmful data you inject via the [[C5]] metadata will be deserialized. As the file extension is not checked when PHP reads a stream, it does not matter that the file uses an image extension." => 'Caranya: unggah berkas polyglot [[C2]]/[[C0]] (berkas [[C1]] menyamar sebagai gambar [[C3]] berisi metadata [[C5]]), lalu arahkan fungsi berkas target untuk membukanya melalui [[C4]].',
    'As long as the class of the object is supported by the website, both the [[C0]] and [[C1]] magic methods can be invoked in this way, allowing you to potentially kick off a gadget chain using this technique.' => 'Selama kelasnya ada di kode target, [[C0]] maupun [[C1]] otomatis terpanggil untuk memicu gadget chain.',
    'This inventive technique was featured in our Top 10 web hacking techniques of 2018.' => 'Teknik ini termasuk dalam 10 teknik peretasan web terbaik tahun 2018.',
    'Top 10 web hacking techniques of 2018' => 'Top 10 teknik peretasan web 2018',
    'Exploiting deserialization using memory corruption' => 'Mengeksploitasi deserialisasi melalui memory corruption',
    'Even without the use of gadget chains, it is still possible to exploit insecure deserialization. If all else fails, there are often publicly documented memory corruption vulnerabilities that can be exploited via insecure deserialization. These typically lead to remote code execution.' => 'Jika tidak ada gadget chain yang cocok, bug memory corruption di implementasi deserialisasi runtime sendiri kadang dapat dimanfaatkan.',
    "Deserialization methods, such as PHP's [[C0]] are rarely hardened against these kinds of attacks, and expose a huge amount of attack surface. This is not always considered a vulnerability in its own right because these methods are not intended to handle user-controllable input in the first place." => 'Parser seperti [[C0]] umumnya tidak dirancang aman menghadapi input biner/string jahat di luar kontrak tepercaya.',
];
